WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.390
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
What's up, everyone?

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.765
Thanks for checking
out This Week

00:00:02.765 --> 00:00:05.192
in Cloud, where we serve
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:05.192 --> 00:00:07.650
You probably already know that
Google Docs is a great place

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.710
to collaborate, but now you can
use the flexibility of an API

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.810
to do even more.

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.310
Whether it's importing docs
from a content management system

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:17.010
or programmatically adding and
templatizing existing docs,

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.800
find the demos and code samples
that you need to get started,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.220
and see examples of it in
action at the Docs API website.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.690
What will you build?

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.922
Google boasts a high-quality
private global network

00:00:26.922 --> 00:00:28.380
that you can use
to keep your cloud

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.030
applications running smoothly.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.772
With the launch of Google
Cloud's Network Service Tiers,

00:00:32.772 --> 00:00:34.230
you can now optimize
your workloads

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.030
for performance and cost.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.850
Are you running a job where
every millisecond counts?

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.202
Use the Premium Tier to
minimize the number of hops.

00:00:41.202 --> 00:00:43.410
But if you're running a more
cost-sensitive workload,

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.360
or you're not as concerned
with network speed,

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.550
save some cash by using
the Standard Tier.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.530
Start customizing your
projects and workloads

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:51.353
by choosing your
network tiers today.

00:00:51.353 --> 00:00:53.520
| course, if you want to
learn more about networking

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.320
and show off your
skills, Google has just

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.760
rolled out a new certification--

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.470
Cloud Network Engineer.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.870
Check out this great blog post
from a solutions architect

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.610
who made the leap from
networking on prem

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:03.827
to the cloud.

00:01:03.827 --> 00:01:05.910
Tom shares tips on how to
stay highly sought-after

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:07.500
in an ever-changing landscape.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.350
So study up, and get certified.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.630
If you're one of the millions
who already uses Box,

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.047
get ready to see
what happens when

00:01:14.047 --> 00:01:16.827
you take advantage of the new
Google ML services integration.

00:01:16.827 --> 00:01:18.660
Upload a batch of files,
and watch Google ML

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.033
do all the sorting
and tagging for you.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.200
Want to see it for yourself?

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.908
Follow the code tutorial
we've linked to,

00:01:23.908 --> 00:01:27.840
and have a fully functioning Box
integration running in minutes.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.930
Do you or someone you know
have to deal with customers?

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:33.420
If so, you may know how
important customer lifetime

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:36.222
value is and the challenges
of trying to predict it.

00:01:36.222 --> 00:01:37.680
We've got a great
solutions article

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.138
that explains how to model this
value with machine learning

00:01:40.138 --> 00:01:42.510
and walks you through how
to implement and host it.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.593
Get your hands on it, and
try it out for yourself.

00:01:44.593 --> 00:01:46.677
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:46.677 --> 00:01:48.540
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.740
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.370
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:53.720
We'll see you in the cloud.

